# ── Generated artifact dumps (added 2026-07-25) ────────────────────────────
# These sat untracked for weeks and made `git status` unreadable, which is why
# the tree looked "50 files dirty" when only ~20 were real work. All regenerable;
# none referenced from v2/src (checked by grep before ignoring).

# Root brand-assets/ is generator output, not the kit. The real, committed kit is
# v2/public/brand/goods/ (landed 3bfc455). Regenerate: tools/generate_goods_brand_kit.py
# NOTE the leading slash on these: a pattern with no internal "/" matches a dir of
# that name at EVERY level, so bare `outputs/` would also swallow wiki/outputs/.
/brand-assets/
/archive/legacy-brand-assets/

# Deck-export artifacts for the superseded .pen decks. The canonical deck spine is
# v2/public/deck-slides/slides-source.html; render with scripts/render-deck.mjs
design/exports/
design/funder-pathways-deck-assets/
design/funder-pathways-deck-export.html
design/funder-pathways-slide-crop.html

# Rendered model diagrams. Keep the .mmd source in git, drop the renders.
diagrams/*.png
diagrams/*.svg
diagrams/*.pdf

# Slide/print exports (PPTX, one-off PDFs). The deck and leave-behind PDFs that
# ARE canonical live under v2/public/deck-slides/ and v2/public/leave-behind/.
/outputs/
v2/snow-dash-print-v2.pdf

# Unreferenced image staging under v2/public (nothing in v2/src points at either).
v2/public/images/_drafts/
v2/public/strategy/

# Miro export dumps: hash-named PNGs, not documents. The .md files in wiki/outputs
# ARE real deliverables and stay tracked.
wiki/outputs/miro-community-model-assets/
wiki/outputs/*.png

# v2/sites/goods-voices is its OWN git repository. Left untracked, `git add -A`
# commits it as a bare gitlink with no .gitmodules, which clones as an empty dir.
# Ignored so that cannot happen. If it should ship with this repo, make it a real
# submodule instead of removing this line.
v2/sites/

# ── Design source + generated audit dumps (added 2026-07-25) ─────────────────
# Pencil .pen files are encrypted binaries: they diff as noise, bloat every
# clone, and no code reads them (the Pencil editor opens them from disk). Per
# the standing rule, big media stays out of git and goes to Supabase Storage.
# NOTE: design/goods-theory-of-change*.pen are already tracked on main and are
# deliberately left tracked, so this ignore does not delete them.
*.pen

# audit/*.json is script output: build-inventory.py writes goods-media-inventory
# .json, build-mapping.py reads it and writes goods-el-mapping.json. Keep the
# scripts, regenerate the data.
audit/*.json

# ── Funder quotes, invoices and commitment paper (added 2026-08-02) ──────────
# These carry a funder's name, a live dollar figure and our ABN, and they land
# in the repo root by accident when someone drops one in to be read. Xero is the
# system of record for a quote or an invoice; GHL carries the ask and its status.
# The repo should hold neither. QU0014.pdf reached the root this way.
Quote *.pdf
Invoice *.pdf
INV-*.pdf
QU-*.pdf

# GOC entity model: the workbook is a BUILD ARTIFACT, not source.
# Regenerate with tools/build-goc-answered-workbook.py, push with tools/push-xlsx-to-gsheet.py.
# Binaries do not diff, and a committed .xlsx nobody can regenerate is worse than none.
deliverables/*.xlsx
deliverables/*.pptx
tools/.gsheet-targets.json
.venv-sheets/

# ── Review and QA screenshots (added 2026-08-03) ─────────────────────────────
# Standing rule: no large media in git, not even LFS. The 2026-07-29 web pitch
# audit alone is ~9MB of PNGs against 7 markdown files. Keep the findings, which
# are text and diff cleanly; drop the screenshots, which do neither.
thoughts/shared/reviews/**/*.png
v2/design-qa-evidence/

# ── GOC entity model build artifacts (mirrors the rules on main) ─────────────
deliverables/*.xlsx
deliverables/*.pptx
# Emitted from v2/src/lib/cost-model/community-model.ts by tools/emit-community-model.ts.
# Untracked on purpose: a committed copy that drifts from the model is worse than an
# absent one, and the workbook generator fails loudly with the regenerate command when
# it is missing rather than falling back to a stale file.
deliverables/community-model.json
tools/.gsheet-targets.json
.venv-sheets/
